<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Asia-Pacific - Latest headlines and news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage of political, social and geostrategic issues across Asia and the Pacific, including those affecting China, Japan, South Korea, North Korea, India, Pakistan and Australia.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e9ea220d22d1cd76d98f1c7dd29c9866ff881f0c7fb63b458c55aa3a7a91c65c</id><updated>2026-09-15T05:05:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas--85ad9b6b4b9f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'What makes China work despite the pain in society?' asks analyst Dan Wang</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5d33f89de6b1133707b67c5afd8b7277a413ac074c350709c0ffa1490b1f679</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T13:30:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang--d40c2ced80a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/what-makes-china-work-despite-the-pain-in-society-asks-analyst-dan-wang" /><summary type="html">In this edition of Perspective, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval speaks to Dan Wang, a China expert whose book ‘Breakneck:  China’s Quest to Engineer the Future’ is a New York Times bestseller. It takes a close look at Chinese life and draws from Wang’s own ten years of living there. Wang says the China and the US are some of the most similar people in the world, as they are both hustlers and take shortcuts.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>Climate catastrophe leaves Nepal mourning while the search for the missing continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:37e27908b2c9bf83f79b74bbee12b65eb87cd1026b97dfd5de9d83b117d3d0de</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T12:43:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues--40d634ca2dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260914-climate-catastrophe-leaves-nepal-mourning-while-the-search-for-the-missing-continues" /><summary type="html">The himalayan flash flood that devastated northern Nepal on August 26 was an unprecedented disaster. The death toll continues to rise, with nearly 1,400 people now confirmed dead and 5,130 still missing, including around 600 foreign nationals from 35 countries.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Rescuers resume search for 129 missing after ferry capsized</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2dadb96f5fef0ecf17515d9ab038cf1eb4d7a5f5d7cbef61d32a64a5bbf0b00</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T08:57:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized--3f97e7973f03.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260914-indonesia-rescuers-resume-search-for-129-missing-after-ferry-capsized" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of Indonesian rescuers including the coast guard and the navy raced on Monday to board a passenger ship that capsized in the Java Sea over the weekend as they searched for 129 people still missing, officials said, with the confirmed death toll at six.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia intensifies search for more than 120 missing after ferry capsizes in Java Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:998e57b5beede5b80c3c96cd14390dd1aa64c9d36dc1b73894ceb33b4aa94fa5</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T06:14:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-indonesia-intensifies-search-missing-after-ferry-capsizes-java-sea--d6966a9b01a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-indonesia-intensifies-search-missing-after-ferry-capsizes-java-sea" /><summary type="html">Indonesian rescue teams on Monday deployed specialised underwater teams and navy-operated underwater drones as the search for more than 120 people missing in the Virgo Transport 8 ferry capsizing intensified.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey detains dozens in raids of bars, homes in crackdown on LGBTQ community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e93f8b5e622ef2053aa848579336b4d6d5746a52fd8dc78db4b16807874932ee</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T19:41:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-turkey-detains-dozens-in-raids-of-bars-homes-in-crackdown-on-lgbtq-community--d3deee7e6ee0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-turkey-detains-dozens-in-raids-of-bars-homes-in-crackdown-on-lgbtq-community" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities on Sunday launched raids on gay bars, nightclubs, LGBTQ association offices and activists' homes in a sweeping crackdown in several cities as part of the government's "My Family is Safe" operations, Turkey's justice minister said. More than 60 people were arrested, according to the state news agency, in raids condemned by human rights groups.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c69ec432d9de0fb5ec131e3528328793906ba69f9ca2dfc32afb40b582beafbb</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days--bcdea8ab2589.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days" /><summary type="html">At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit: What came out of the New Delhi meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac3df8e92751009b23939335832fb43a2c1580fa53d28a4dc38ae57615c6416</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:27:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting--2d7ab6cb6280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit in New Delhi ended with a joint declaration calling for greater Global South influence in global governance and urging restraint in the Middle East. The gathering also served as a platform for one-to-one diplomacy, with leaders holding a series of bilateral meetings aimed at easing regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Second life': Nepal hydropower tunnel survivor recalls ordeal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd469b4e66c2449346cc7072667967b0fc0ad8131300f368555dbfa190e9237f</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T04:17:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal--bac6c1a764d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260913-second-life-nepal-hydropower-tunnel-survivor-recalls-ordeal" /><summary type="html">Nepali hydropower worker Sanjay Sah survived in total darkness inside a tunnel flooded by the deadly flash flood that struck the China-Nepal border on August 26, drinking muddy water and praying that rescuers would find him. The survivor, who was rescued on September 4, recalls the 10 days he spent stranded.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS leaders call for 'maximum restraint' as Middle East war threatens unity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a079cfcf3e31c40e6a4d56c11b1f67e95933e9cdfb84f8af6b0ff64bd7e5610a</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T06:51:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran--19071f618e81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260912-brics-summit-set-to-be-dominated-by-wars-in-ukraine-and-iran" /><summary type="html">BRICS leaders meeting in New Delhi on Saturday unanimously adopted a joint declaration expressing "deep concern" over the war in the Middle East and urging maximum restraint. The statement was seen as indirect criticism of US and Israeli strikes on Iranian nuclear facilities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hate speech against Rohingya refugees on the rise in Malaysia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24cb85495c4370ddfc4225fdeeed7b82d3fc07ba4c31959338393f2f08184960</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T14:34:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260911-hate-speech-rohingya-refugees-rise-malaysia--dd6c980fdaa8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-observers/20260911-hate-speech-rohingya-refugees-rise-malaysia" /><summary type="html">Hostile social media content, disinformation campaigns, and a petition calling for their expulsion: in Malaysia, a wave of hate speech has been targeting Rohingya refugees, a Muslim minority driven out of Myanmar. The rising hostility has already led to the eviction of more than 100 people from a village and forced the temporary closure of schools serving refugee children.</summary><category term="The Observers" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: Rescue efforts continue in the aftermath of a flash flooding disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ab2435ce0673ca67645a6bc31c4ea27b117af6b0aa85a0016aabe547b0c6eb3</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T09:41:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster--6bc8de0c3bb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260911-nepal-rescue-efforts-continue-in-the-aftermath-of-a-flash-flooding-disaster" /><summary type="html">Two weeks after the devastating flash floods, the number of dead and missing continues to rise. At Kathmandu’s public hospital, as well as outside the military base in Bidur, hundreds of photographs of missing people have been put up. Hundreds of families come forward, hoping for news – good or bad – of one or more loved ones. A race against time is underway: helping survivors, finding those still alive and identifying the victims. Rescue teams have been carrying out repeated helicopter flights, as air access is now the only way to reach remote areas cut off from the rest of the world. Civil society has also mobilised, particularly Nepal’s Generation Z. From Kathmandu to Betrawati, FRANCE 24's reporters Alban Alvarez and Fantine Dantzer accompanied a humanitarian convoy along one of the country’s most treacherous roads.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>Putin arrives in India for BRICS summit set to be dominated by Middle East, Ukraine wars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bb599d1ec9dce53bf8eb33ac0f3ef5ad66a4eed91a97a33ec16a2e3329a77911</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T02:08:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars--f89644d9206b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-putin-xi-india-brics-summit-ukraine-middle-east-wars" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived in New Delhi on Friday for a two-day BRICS summit expected to focus on wars in Ukraine and the Middle East and economic challenges. Putin and Iran’s President Masoud Pezeshkian are due to meet Prime Minister Narendra Modi, while China’s Xi Jinping is also expected to hold talks.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong court sentences Tiananmen vigil activists to between 5 and 7 years in jail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:60150780e7c8fc50178ec0bb63eb45453e7ed8ec3a9421cd04c6369821824322</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T01:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-hong-kong-court-sentences-tiananmen-vigil-activists-to-between-5-and-7-years-in-jail--c84217a1e5ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260911-hong-kong-court-sentences-tiananmen-vigil-activists-to-between-5-and-7-years-in-jail" /><summary type="html">Three activists who had held annual vigils commemorating the Tiananmen Square crackdown were sentenced to between five and seven years in prison Friday for calling for an "end to one-party dictatorship". Prosecutors had argued that China's constitution enshrines the primacy of the Communist Party.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Seoul spy agency unveils potential new heir to North Korea’s Kim Jong-un</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66876ece54a26c010f37be164b195ef5b9ab11005772064eb0d521c8192da007</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T09:07:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-north-korea-succession-in-question-as-seoul-spy-agency-unveils-potential-new-heir--f81067078d99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-north-korea-succession-in-question-as-seoul-spy-agency-unveils-potential-new-heir" /><summary type="html">A South Korean spy agency on Thursday revealed that North Korean leader Kim Jong-un could have a child born before his chosen successor, daughter Kim Ju Ae, which raises questions about succession. Information about the Kim dynasty is scarce and often difficult to verify.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Deadly Philippines ferry fire leaves dozens missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef1f737f9dbb7a89ea903e511532b5e69ca3d8f64a889a9a609a0532f191af02</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T01:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-at-least-five-killed-87-missing-after-ferry-fire-in-philippines--9984cd2fa739.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260910-at-least-five-killed-87-missing-after-ferry-fire-in-philippines" /><summary type="html">At least five people died and dozens were unaccounted for Thursday after a ferry caught fire off the Philippine island province of Palawan, with 43 passengers and crew rescued so far. Coast guard teams continued search and rescue operations as officials worked to establish what happened.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>The world's third global aerospace market: India's civil aviation sector takes off</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:67e489503b8beb5664491d8da7e4d4a7b8993fbb83e175aab0c857fe2238b7e6</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T12:34:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260909-the-world-s-third-global-aerospace-market-india-s-civil-aviation-sector-takes-off--663d5050bc0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260909-the-world-s-third-global-aerospace-market-india-s-civil-aviation-sector-takes-off" /><summary type="html">The aviation sector is one of the India's strongest-performing industries. More than 70 airports have been built over the past decade, and the country counts over 400 million air passengers annually. In just ten years, India has become the world's third-largest aviation market, behind China and the United States.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Spoiler alert: AI in cinema 'just a tool, won’t replace actors and human beings'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:194cfc1307fcb11e91c2dbf5c885fd8c7714b4487346923080e4197684eceb89</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:11:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1--59df42aa2e9d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260908-spoiler-alert-ai-in-cinema-just-a-tool-won-t-replace-actors-and-human-beings-1" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome film producer Lahoucine Grimich. He challenges the prevailing narrative that cinema is an industry in existential crisis. While acknowledging that viewing habits have dramatically shifted since the pandemic, he argues that streaming platforms, public support and theatrical exhibition are not competing forces. As demonstrated in the French model, they form parts of an interconnected financing ecosystem in which cinema can adapt without ever abandoning the big screen. He frames filmmaking as a form of cultural sovereignty: societies need films not simply as entertainment, but to recognise themselves and to create what he calls “new imaginaries.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal rescuers race to free dozens trapped in hydropower tunnels</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:788388e8af01fedc99f2fa7a7344b6b520d4cf41efadad66a0245e5477892583</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:51:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260908-nepal-rescuers-race-to-free-dozens-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels--d5355493ce50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260908-nepal-rescuers-race-to-free-dozens-trapped-in-hydropower-tunnels" /><summary type="html">Authorities in Nepal on Tuesday said that rescuers are focusing on three hydropower project tunnels where they believe dozens of workers could be trapped. The announcement came two weeks after ​a devastating ‌flood killed that hundreds and left thousands missing in the Himalayan country and in ⁠neighbouring China's Tibet region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Eight airports in Indonesia suspend operations after volcanic eruption</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5907867bac198ea748bda5cbe4c9f1e2317147f0e7d00713d473002efb8a8c13</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T06:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260906-six-airports-in-indonesia-suspend-operations-after-volcanic-eruption--3d1cdb1ba565.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260906-six-airports-in-indonesia-suspend-operations-after-volcanic-eruption" /><summary type="html">Eight airports in Indonesia, including Jakarta's main international airport, suspended operations Sunday after the erupting Anak Krakatoa volcano spewed clouds of ash across the archipelago. Geologists said that the latest series of eruptions does not have the potential to trigger a tsunami at this time.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>'I don't know if I'm dreaming': Rebuilding lives after Nepal's devastating floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a4e741587a14e6975765b7af72e84a49b0d85d7184e158c32d240d665cf81b5</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T10:16:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260905-i-dont-know-if-im-dreaming-rebuilding-lives-after-nepal-devastating-floods--411c987116c0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260905-i-dont-know-if-im-dreaming-rebuilding-lives-after-nepal-devastating-floods" /><summary type="html">With thousands of people driven from their homes by a massive flash flood that swept entire villages away, FRANCE 24 visits a school in Nepal's remote Rasuwa district that has been converted to a temporary shelter for the dispossessed.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Himalayan hydropower buildout: Expert says risk management is key</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01964592d8c985dccbbf021c64bfd30790969ec9833746e98dbcd46081a8ad4a</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:34:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260904-rebuilding-after-nepal-flash-floods-expert-says-risk-management-is-key-in-himalayas--1975b47e4597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260904-rebuilding-after-nepal-flash-floods-expert-says-risk-management-is-key-in-himalayas" /><summary type="html">Following devastating floods in Nepal and Tibet, Access Asia takes a closer look at the fragile state of the Himalayan mountains. Dr Arun Bhakta Shrestha, an expert on the environment and risk management in the Himalayas, explains why it's so difficult to detect glacier movements in advance and says that the tragedy could serve as an opportunity to improve the way nations develop infrastructure in the resource-rich region.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods: Two workers pulled alive from tunnel after nine days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b14121e1bccc4565939d650c8c4a5ab064374bcc82c2cb2c29b84fa228bd7d9f</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:54:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-floods-two-workers-pulled-alive-from-tunnel-after-nine-days--5651e62af958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-floods-two-workers-pulled-alive-from-tunnel-after-nine-days" /><summary type="html">Nepal's emergency crews have pulled two workers out of a hydropower tunnel where they had been trapped for nine days. The rescue comes more than a week after flash flooding along the Nepal-Tibet border killed more than 1,200 people. Both men have injuries to their hands and legs and have been airlifted to a hospital in Kathmandu for treatment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Two trapped workers rescued from mud-clogged tunnel 9 days after Nepal floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4816c7640b224f8d783f690c8fc2a99508969d01d10425c095955d6f4c271623</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T10:12:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-two-trapped-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-9-days-after-nepal-floods--395bdff0000d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-two-trapped-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-9-days-after-nepal-floods" /><summary type="html">Nine days after catastrophic floods hit Nepal, hope emerges from the dark as two workers have been rescued from a collapsed tunnel. They are receiving treatment as emergency crews race to find more survivors. The floods killed more than 1,200 people and left over 5,000 missing. An estimated 115 people are still believed trapped in the tunnel.</summary></entry><entry><title>#Nepal: Two flood survivors rescued from hydropower tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b260ff26ac791fcd5f82b87cf072f0a748b7965f534c1f871d5a8327e9d1035</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:38:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-two-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel--4c0fb43a0f62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-two-flood-survivors-rescued-from-hydropower-tunnel" /><summary type="html">In a video posted to social media on September 4, the Nepali #army announced it had rescued two workers trapped in a hydropower tunnel. The rescue brings hope of reaching over a dozen others thought to be trapped inside the tunnel. Both men were flown to a hospital in #Kathmandu. The floods killed more than 1,200 people, and over 5,000 are still missing.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why early warning signs of glacier collapse in Nepal were difficult to detect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:596a89a487b3e750b5ae20d7cdcf7e0e3e6950555b6778a6f2fbb88d04800cec</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:24:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-nepal-why-early-warning-signs-of-glacier-collapse-were-difficult-to-detect--b6433db61383.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-nepal-why-early-warning-signs-of-glacier-collapse-were-difficult-to-detect" /><summary type="html">The glacier collapse that led to devastating flash floods across the Himalayan region of Nepal and its border with the Chinese autonomous region of Tibet on August 26 was preceded by early warning signs, experts say. But monitoring and emergency alert systems in the region are still insufficient to predict such disasters.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>USS Lincoln crew hits the streets of Thailand's Pattaya after nine-month deployment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a5e1cc01f62f951772a1c7c3dcfcd2c1436a9aaa36af35c33efab4e945eae2</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T07:02:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-uss-lincoln-crew-hits-the-streets-of-thailand-pattaya-after-nine-month-deployment--29255ce7fac8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-uss-lincoln-crew-hits-the-streets-of-thailand-pattaya-after-nine-month-deployment" /><summary type="html">US sailors and Marines streamed into the Thai resort city of Pattaya Thursday after a record-breaking nine months at sea. Local police said there had so far been no major incidents connected to the 5,000-strong contingent of US service members, though two sailors were sent back to the ship after a drunken bar brawl.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Two trapped hydropower workers rescued from mud-clogged tunnel in Nepal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34e877053c67088dbde6059dc0484cd8bf4d1a563b57036fb3646941d66877f0</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T05:10:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-two-trapped-hydropower-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-in-nepal--20381ee92342.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260904-two-trapped-hydropower-workers-rescued-from-mud-clogged-tunnel-in-nepal" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams on Friday pulled two hydropower workers free from a tunnel blocked by mud and debris during the massive flood that swept through Nepal in late August. Officials believe that hundreds of workers remain trapped in tunnels connected to hydropower projects throughout the remote Himalayan region.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>‘Fight through darkness, water’: Nepal survivor recounts escape from flood-hit tunnel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b27d20e1bc09f01164dbe9e549dbcf7016b6ef2e434e4fc8d77e7fc2c6153897</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:22:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel--029aa5abd2d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260903-fight-through-darkness-water-nepal-survivor-recounts-escape-from-flood-hit-tunnel" /><summary type="html">A Nepalese worker recounts his harrowing escape from a hydropower project tunnel after last week's devastating flood. Around 900 workers remain trapped in tunnels at six hydroelectric plants in Nepal as the number of missing in the Himalayan disaster rose to 5,624 on Thursday, according to Nepalese and Chinese authorities.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal: How are the hundreds of victims from the floods being identified?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c95efce51cff10397f982764ada49c3424cd0692ef48dc82be0aeb89c383c71c</id><updated>2026-09-14T20:21:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T10:52:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified--61d3ca55ccc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260903-nepal-how-are-the-hundreds-of-victims-from-the-floods-being-identified" /><summary type="html">#Nepal faces a major challenge: identifying the remains that have been found after the #flood that tore through part of the country on August 26, some of which are in an advanced state of decomposition. For #health reasons, the unidentified bodies have begun to be buried. Before each #burial, #DNA samples are taken and an identification number is assigned to each set of remains. Relatives of those reported missing can visit DNA collection centres to provide a sample. Their genetic profile can then be compared with that of the bodies found, in the hope of identifying them. FRANCE 24’s correspondents visited one such centre, set up within the #police #hospital in #Kathmandu.</summary></entry></feed>
